"file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348649" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{t+8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]$ at $t=\\pi ?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(\\pi )=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t=\\pi $ into our function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(\\pi ) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi +8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi +1) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi +8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi +1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\pi+8}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\pi+1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-3),\\,\\sqrt{2t},\\,{t}^{5}⟩$ at $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t=2$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2}-3),\\sqrt{2(2)},{2}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1),\\sqrt{4},{2}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,2,32⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=2$ is the vector $⟨0,2,32⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,2,32⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\sqrt{2},32⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,2,16⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,2,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\sqrt{2},32⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,2,32⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-160776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of $f(t)=2{e}^{t}\\,i+\\sqrt{t+4}\\,j+(t-2)^{4}\\,k$ at $t=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-160776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t=0$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =2{e}^{0}\\,i+\\sqrt{0+4}\\,j+(0-2)^{4}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+16\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=0$ is the vector $2\\,i+2\\,j+16\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-160776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-160776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-160776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\,i+16\\,k"] ["math" "2\\,i+2\\,j+16\\,k"] ["math" "2\\,i+2\\,j-16\\,k"] ["math" "2\\,k"] ["math" "5\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-160776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,i+2\\,j+16\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of $f(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t+1},\\,{t}^{2}-3,\\,1-t⟩$ at $t=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t=1$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =⟨\\sqrt{1+1},{1}^{2}-3,1-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{2},1-3,1-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{2},-2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=1$ is the vector $⟨\\sqrt{2},-2,0⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-161509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,-2,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,4,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\sqrt{2},-2,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\sqrt{2},1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\sqrt{2},2,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-161509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\sqrt{2},-2,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t),\\,\\sqrt{t+3},\\,t-1⟩,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,\\sqrt{4},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348693" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-348693" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348693" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{3}-4},\\,ln\\,(2\\,{e}^{t-2}-1)⟩,$ what is $|r(2)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(2)|=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating the function at $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨cos\\,(\\frac{2\\pi }{2}),\\,\\sqrt{{2}^{3}-4},\\,ln\\,(2\\,{e}^{0}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,\\sqrt{4},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(2)| & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-348690" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-348690" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-75004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,t-3⟩,$ $|r(5)|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-75004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating the function at $t=5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(5) & =⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,5-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{5},\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(5)| & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{5})}^{2}+{(2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5+4} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-75004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-75004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-75004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-75004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩,$ $|r(\\frac{\\pi }{3})|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating the function at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(\\frac{\\pi }{3})| & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-123284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨4{sin}^{2}⁡(5t),\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)⟩,$ $|r(\\frac{\\pi }{3})|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating the function at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =⟨4{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3}),\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(\\frac{\\pi }{3})| & =\\sqrt{{(3)}^{2}+{(5)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a"} {"question" "q-123218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{17}"] ["math" "34"] ["math" "\\sqrt{15}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{34}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "q-123218" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{34}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "7392cb01eeef749f2c393f55fc87bf7047defec255e5823e09e73ffa1c3a5902"} {"question" "e-12450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle 6t, 2t^2-1\\rangle,$ calculate $\\mathbf r (3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/example-12450.json" "file_sha256" "100f404f788a4a4142e3b5bd271a158dfc819352b53235767b3f0e249389a9bd"} {"question" "e-12450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We substitute $t=3$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨6(3),\\,2(3)^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18,\\,17⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/example-12450.json" "file_sha256" "100f404f788a4a4142e3b5bd271a158dfc819352b53235767b3f0e249389a9bd"} {"question" "e-12452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the vector function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\cos t, \\: \\sin t, \\: t \\right\\rangle$ at $t = \\pi.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/example-12452.json" "file_sha256" "7661219b48d572039943434dd824270e4ab8ba07d787838feb01e049ee2a509d"} {"question" "e-12452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi ⟩=⟨-1,0,\\pi \\,⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle.$\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\pi \\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/example-12452.json" "file_sha256" "7661219b48d572039943434dd824270e4ab8ba07d787838feb01e049ee2a509d"} {"question" "e-12451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(4\\right)\\right|$ given that $\\mathbf r(t)  = \\left\\langle 2-t, 2\\sqrt{t}, \\, t-1\\right\\rangle,$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/example-12451.json" "file_sha256" "eeff3ca2bffbe61ae328925d86f3299f18f4706eb3ec09ae55ad2a066028b0e0"} {"question" "e-12451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating the function at $t=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(4) & =⟨2-4,\\,2\\sqrt{4},\\,4-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(4)| & =\\sqrt{{(-2)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}+{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/example-12451.json" "file_sha256" "eeff3ca2bffbe61ae328925d86f3299f18f4706eb3ec09ae55ad2a066028b0e0"}] "usage" {"e-12451" [] "q-75004" [] "q-50083" [] "e-12450" [] "e-12452" []} "basis" 1267 "retractions" [[17592186069327 :question/problem "Given that $r(t) = ⟨t^{2}, 3t^{3}⟩$, calculate $r(2)$."] [17592186068380 :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r (t) = \\langle 6t, 2t^2-1\\rangle$, calculate $\\mathbf r (3)$."] [17592186068380 :question/worked-solution "We substitute $t=3$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr(3) &= ⟨6(3), 2(3)^{2} - 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨18, 17⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186068382 :question/problem "Find the value of the vector function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\cos t, \\: \\sin t, \\: t \\right\\rangle$ at $t = \\pi$."] [17592186068382 :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(π) &= ⟨\\cos π, \\sin π, π⟩ = ⟨ - 1, 0, π⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle$.\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ π\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186068381 :question/problem "Find $\\left|\\mathbf r\\left(4\\right)\\right|$ given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\left\\langle 2-t, 2\\sqrt{t}, \\, t-1\\right\\rangle$,"] [17592186068381 :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr(4) &= ⟨2 - 4, 2\\sqrt{4}, 4 - 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2, 4, 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid r(4) \\mid &= \\sqrt{(-2)^{2} + (4)^{2} + (3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4 + 16 + 9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{29}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186067494 17592186067495 17592186067496 17592186067497 17592186067498 17592186268615 17592186268616 17592186268617 17592186268618 17592186268619] "immutable_fields" [[17592186067493 :answer-field/correct] [17592186067493 :answer-field/id] [17592186067493 :answer-field/key] [17592186067493 :answer-field/type] [17592186268614 :answer-field/correct] [17592186268614 :answer-field/id] [17592186268614 :answer-field/key] [17592186268614 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
